On Oct 8, 11:26 am, rpresser <rpres...@gmail.com> wrote:
> The patch I'm thinking of would allow multiple bones files to be saved
> for each level.
>[...]
> It doesn't seem technically too difficult to implement. Is it too
> meaningless to worry about?

     I suspect that it'll be harder than you think.  Some of
the platforms don't provide a supported way to do wildcarded
file lookup, so you'd need to step through each possible file
name looking for one that exists, or else rename the remainder
after consuming one from the front or middle of the list.  And
even with wildcard lookup, there'll be the possibility of race
conditions where multiple processes are simultaneously trying
to collect the set of available files or use the same file.
With the current arrangement, if one process locks a particular
bones file, other processes can assume that it's gone and just
make a new level instead.  With a change like this, they'd
need to wait until the first process has completed its use of
that level's bones.  Or perhaps they could behave the old way
and just miss out on bones during the rare times when two or
more players are entering the same new level at the same time.



